<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ezequiel Zamora</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ezequiel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a> was a Venezuelan soldier and Liberal leader in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-war">Federal War</a> of 1859–1863. Championing federalism and land for the poor, he won the decisive Battle of Santa Inés in December 1859 but was killed by a bullet during the siege of San Carlos in January 1860; he was later honoured as a popular hero, notably by the Chávez government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ezequiel-zamora.jpg" alt="Ezequiel Zamora" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilfredor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ezequiel_Zamora_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
